1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
[English subtitles are available]

2
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:02,720
Since you can't say it,

3
00:00:02,810 --> 00:00:04,220
I'll say it for you.

4
00:00:04,310 --> 00:00:05,230
That guy showed up

5
00:00:05,320 --> 00:00:06,460
because he wants to make Hsieh Tien-ti

6
00:00:06,550 --> 00:00:09,190
disappear from this world once more.

7
00:00:28,290 --> 00:00:29,250
How did we...

8
00:00:29,340 --> 00:00:29,910
You...

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,500
This place is...

10
00:00:43,470 --> 00:00:45,310
The weather is nice, it looks hot.

11
00:00:45,450 --> 00:00:46,990
Yes, it was so hot that day.

12
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:56,580
Make way!

13
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:01,590
Has the family been notified?

14
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:03,620
Yes, we've notified them.

15
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:17,960
This is a Reflection of Time.

16
00:01:40,090 --> 00:01:41,370
Tien-ti!

17
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:43,960
Are you okay?

18
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:47,039
I saw a lot of strange things.

19
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:49,240
What did you see?

20
00:01:49,950 --> 00:01:51,970
I saw that I was in the hospital.

21
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:54,789
I was talking to a girl I didn't know.

22
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:58,039
But I couldn't hear clearly
what we were saying.

23
00:01:58,530 --> 00:01:59,710
When I wanted to walk forward,

24
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:01,610
something happened to the girl.

25
00:02:01,740 --> 00:02:05,210
A lot of people pushed her
to the emergency room.

26
00:02:05,350 --> 00:02:07,550
Then I went somewhere else.

27
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:08,949
That place...

28
00:02:09,750 --> 00:02:12,830
I heard a woman singing.

29
00:02:14,230 --> 00:02:16,350
Then there were a lot of people

30
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:19,160
fainting one by one right in front of me.

31
00:02:21,320 --> 00:02:22,860
You saw the Reflection of Time again.

32
00:02:36,630 --> 00:02:38,790
Tien-ti! Stop right there.

33
00:02:48,950 --> 00:02:50,930
So you already knew.

34
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:01,360
I warned you.

35
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:03,560
Don't read my mind as you wish.

36
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:06,940
I'm really curious.

37
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:07,780
Did you really come back

38
00:03:07,910 --> 00:03:09,190
just to correct

39
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:10,640
the cause and effect?

40
00:03:11,340 --> 00:03:12,840
If that was the case,

41
00:03:12,930 --> 00:03:14,200
why didn't you just stop 'Orad

42
00:03:14,290 --> 00:03:16,760
when he kissed Hsieh Tien-ti?

43
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,960
Or could it be

44
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:20,410
that you,

45
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:21,860
who specialize

46
00:03:21,990 --> 00:03:23,660
in keeping Kakarayan's secrets,

47
00:03:23,750 --> 00:03:25,640
have decided to expose everything?

48
00:03:33,740 --> 00:03:36,860
Wu Yi-han, you're so annoying.

49
00:03:36,950 --> 00:03:40,160
I went to the next spot with him,

50
00:03:40,250 --> 00:03:41,829
then my phone died.

51
00:03:41,920 --> 00:03:43,590
When we went back,

52
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:45,270
you two were already gone.

53
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:48,790
[Hsieh Tien-ti,
we've known each other for so long.]

54
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:51,340
[You really don't have to say more.]

55
00:03:51,430 --> 00:03:54,070
[I trust you 100%.]

56
00:03:54,150 --> 00:03:56,270
You'd better be.

57
00:03:56,350 --> 00:03:58,470
[Okay, I trust that you and my darling]

58
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:00,180
[really didn't go anywhere.]

59
00:04:00,270 --> 00:04:01,370
[Don't worry about me.]

60
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:04,140
[Have a good time with my darling.]

61
00:04:04,270 --> 00:04:05,550
[♫ Let me hold you ♫]

62
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:07,180
[♫ Let darling hold you ♫]

63
00:04:07,270 --> 00:04:08,540
[Bye.]

64
00:04:10,260 --> 00:04:12,810
That crazy girl.
Why did she suddenly start singing?

65
00:04:12,900 --> 00:04:13,780
Are you done?

66
00:04:13,910 --> 00:04:14,750
Yes, I'm done.

67
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:16,420
What did she say?

68
00:04:17,779 --> 00:04:19,810
A bunch of nonsense, so just ignore her.

69
00:04:21,390 --> 00:04:22,620
Let's go.

70
00:04:24,650 --> 00:04:26,760
Aren't we going to see the professor?

71
00:04:24,690 --> 00:04:28,740
[Do not cross]

72
00:04:26,850 --> 00:04:28,170
Does he live here?

73
00:04:29,050 --> 00:04:30,370
Isn't he a Kawas?

74
00:04:30,450 --> 00:04:32,430
Why does he live

75
00:04:32,570 --> 00:04:35,030
in such a strange place?

76
00:04:35,870 --> 00:04:37,800
No one knows what's going on in his mind.

77
00:04:39,030 --> 00:04:39,780
But because of that,

78
00:04:39,870 --> 00:04:40,790
he might know

79
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:41,850
why you suddenly obtained

80
00:04:41,940 --> 00:04:43,610
the power to teleport

81
00:04:44,659 --> 00:04:45,190
and are able to see

82
00:04:45,280 --> 00:04:47,170
the Reflection of Time
which you shouldn't have seen.

83
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:54,210
Open up, it's me.

84
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:58,830
Hello, are you taking a break?

85
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:00,550
No.

86
00:05:03,410 --> 00:05:05,610
I'm looking for my friend who lives here.

87
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:07,850
The guest already checked out
this morning.

88
00:05:09,350 --> 00:05:10,360
He checked out?

89
00:05:11,280 --> 00:05:12,740
So do you need a room?

90
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:13,750
No.

91
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:14,890
We really don't need it.

92
00:05:15,460 --> 00:05:16,170
Thank you.

93
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,020
[Your call will be transferred
to voicemail.]

94
00:05:22,240 --> 00:05:23,870
I can't reach him on his cell phone.

95
00:05:27,430 --> 00:05:29,940
Where are we going to find him now?

96
00:05:30,780 --> 00:05:31,610
I don't know.

97
00:05:32,670 --> 00:05:34,470
That guy is very elusive.

98
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:37,110
If it wasn't because I was able to see
the Reflection of Time previously,

99
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:39,570
no one could have found him.

100
00:05:42,170 --> 00:05:44,850
Should we tell the driver...

101
00:05:45,909 --> 00:05:48,730
We can't just wander around like this.

102
00:05:49,470 --> 00:05:53,790
[Radio]

103
00:05:50,130 --> 00:05:52,330
[Hello, listeners.]

104
00:05:52,420 --> 00:05:55,409
[Welcome to another session
of "Hui's Small Talk."]

105
00:05:55,500 --> 00:05:56,690
[Yes, you heard me right.]

106
00:05:56,820 --> 00:05:59,200
[By "small," I mean "simple."]

107
00:05:59,330 --> 00:06:02,280
[It's not the "small" as in size.]

108
00:06:02,370 --> 00:06:03,640
Driver, can you turn up the volume?

109
00:06:03,730 --> 00:06:04,040
Okay.

110
00:06:04,130 --> 00:06:06,240
[This is a story of the god of rain
saving a woman.]

111
00:06:06,370 --> 00:06:07,560
[Yesterday, we stopped after learning]

112
00:06:07,650 --> 00:06:09,670
[that the god of rain has lost his powers]

113
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:10,900
[to protect]

114
00:06:10,990 --> 00:06:12,970
[the little girl he loves.]

115
00:06:13,060 --> 00:06:15,520
[He gave up his powers.]

116
00:06:15,610 --> 00:06:17,460
-The god of rain?
[-But in the face of the threat]

117
00:06:17,550 --> 00:06:19,130
-Little girl?
[-of the Witch of Destruction,]

118
00:06:19,220 --> 00:06:21,290
[if the god of rain
wants to regain his powers,]

119
00:06:21,420 --> 00:06:23,660
[the only way]

120
00:06:23,750 --> 00:06:26,740
[is to kiss the girl.]

121
00:06:32,020 --> 00:06:34,130
-I think we found him.
[-But the girl]

122
00:06:34,260 --> 00:06:35,850
-Do you guys know the host?
[-can't do anything either.]

123
00:06:36,730 --> 00:06:38,490
Do you know him, sir?

124
00:06:38,580 --> 00:06:39,900
Of course.

125
00:06:39,980 --> 00:06:42,140
I'm a huge fan of Mr. Immortal.

126
00:06:42,270 --> 00:06:43,370
Do you like him too?

127
00:06:43,500 --> 00:06:45,260
We love him.

128
00:06:45,350 --> 00:06:46,320
Who loves him?

129
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:48,340
I play a lot of chess with him.

130
00:06:48,430 --> 00:06:49,710
Do you want to hear it live?

131
00:06:50,850 --> 00:06:51,640
-Yes, please.
[-Why are you]

132
00:06:52,220 --> 00:06:53,710
-Okay, I'll take you there.
[-so slow-witted?]

133
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:56,040
[It's okay. Just give it a try.]

134
00:06:56,130 --> 00:06:56,970
He's dead meat.

135
00:06:57,060 --> 00:06:59,610
[Kiss her. Go on.]

136
00:06:59,700 --> 00:07:02,690
You mean that Witch of Destruction

137
00:07:02,820 --> 00:07:04,760
is the god of rain's ex-girlfriend?

138
00:07:04,890 --> 00:07:06,560
Is it for real?

139
00:07:07,130 --> 00:07:08,280
It seems that you are really into it.

140
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:09,240
Of course I am.

141
00:07:09,330 --> 00:07:10,560
Let me tell you.

142
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:11,840
There are two options.

143
00:07:11,930 --> 00:07:13,070
The first

144
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:15,400
is to be sure to tune in
to my show tomorrow.

145
00:07:15,490 --> 00:07:16,810
The second way is...

146
00:07:16,990 --> 00:07:17,780
All right, everyone.

147
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:19,580
Self-drawn win!

148
00:07:19,670 --> 00:07:20,020
No way

149
00:07:20,110 --> 00:07:21,300
This can't be.

150
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:22,490
Darn it!

151
00:07:22,570 --> 00:07:23,100
You played tricks.

152
00:07:23,190 --> 00:07:24,160
Pay money to me. What tricks?

153
00:07:24,250 --> 00:07:25,700
Come on, pay up. Stop talking.

154
00:07:25,790 --> 00:07:26,400
Why are you talking so much?

155
00:07:26,490 --> 00:07:27,550
Mr. Immortal.

156
00:07:27,630 --> 00:07:29,220
I brought your fans here to see you.

157
00:07:29,310 --> 00:07:29,790
I have fans?

158
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:30,760
Yes.

159
00:07:30,850 --> 00:07:31,990
How is the game going today?

160
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:33,130
I actually have fans?

161
00:07:34,450 --> 00:07:35,330
I didn't know I had fans.

162
00:07:35,420 --> 00:07:37,180
Stop talking and pay up.

163
00:07:38,190 --> 00:07:39,380
Why is it you?

164
00:07:40,310 --> 00:07:42,460
Hi.

165
00:07:42,590 --> 00:07:45,320
Don't look at me like that.

166
00:07:45,409 --> 00:07:46,330
Especially you.

167
00:07:46,420 --> 00:07:47,300
That cold look in your eyes

168
00:07:47,390 --> 00:07:48,800
makes me feel overwhelmed.

169
00:07:48,890 --> 00:07:51,170
It's about to wear me out.

170
00:07:51,310 --> 00:07:52,450
I have my difficulties.

171
00:07:52,540 --> 00:07:55,530
I need to live too.

172
00:07:57,159 --> 00:07:58,170
It was because you told me

173
00:07:58,260 --> 00:07:59,490
that Fali came back.

174
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:00,370
If Fali came back,

175
00:08:00,460 --> 00:08:01,120
my wife who is his secretary

176
00:08:01,250 --> 00:08:02,790
must have come back with him, right?

177
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:03,890
Little girl.

178
00:08:04,020 --> 00:08:05,030
Be the judge here.

179
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:07,280
You must agree
that I had no choice but to run, right?

180
00:08:07,940 --> 00:08:09,130
Who is Fali?

181
00:08:10,930 --> 00:08:12,430
Fali is the head
of the Cause and Effect Correction Bureau.

182
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:13,530
Didn't you know?

183
00:08:13,610 --> 00:08:15,730
He's in charge of the whole bureau.

184
00:08:15,860 --> 00:08:18,760
My wife is his secretary. My Gosh.

185
00:08:18,890 --> 00:08:20,700
What does Fali have to correct?

186
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:23,290
He corrects

187
00:08:23,380 --> 00:08:24,260
all the things

188
00:08:24,350 --> 00:08:26,550
that go against Kakarayan's will.

189
00:08:26,640 --> 00:08:27,120
Like how you...

190
00:08:27,210 --> 00:08:28,880
Hold on.

191
00:08:28,970 --> 00:08:31,210
We came to see you about something else.

192
00:08:32,270 --> 00:08:35,480
Something else made you
come to look for me?

193
00:08:35,610 --> 00:08:37,020
What is it?

194
00:08:38,690 --> 00:08:41,159
Teleportation!

195
00:08:41,240 --> 00:08:42,919
Wait, so you're saying

196
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:43,929
the moment you opened your eyes,

197
00:08:44,020 --> 00:08:45,510
you were teleported somewhere else

198
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:47,620
and you brought 'Orad with you?

199
00:08:49,250 --> 00:08:52,160
This is unbelievable.

200
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:55,500
She's not turning
into a real Kawas, is she?

201
00:08:55,630 --> 00:08:58,670
Goodness. What will you be in charge of?

202
00:08:58,760 --> 00:09:00,430
Will it be beauty?

203
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:02,140
I've been wondering

204
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:06,020
if her powers came from me or Toem.

205
00:09:06,900 --> 00:09:08,260
Judging from what happened today,

206
00:09:08,790 --> 00:09:09,580
it should be from me.

207
00:09:10,150 --> 00:09:12,400
If what you said is true,

208
00:09:13,410 --> 00:09:14,860
that means 'Orad didn't actually
lose his powers.

209
00:09:14,950 --> 00:09:16,710
He just transferred them onto me.

210
00:09:17,890 --> 00:09:19,080
Then what exactly should I do

211
00:09:19,170 --> 00:09:21,060
to return the powers back to him?

212
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:26,120
Haven't I already told you both before?

213
00:09:26,210 --> 00:09:29,420
Take it back the same way you lost it.

214
00:09:34,880 --> 00:09:37,250
Actually, we had already tried that.

215
00:09:37,340 --> 00:09:39,320
You had already tried that?

216
00:09:39,410 --> 00:09:41,390
It didn't work at all.

217
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:45,830
You were playing hard to get,

218
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:47,240
but when you had to get it done,

219
00:09:47,330 --> 00:09:49,400
you managed to do it after all.

220
00:09:49,490 --> 00:09:51,030
Well? How did he do?

221
00:09:51,160 --> 00:09:51,990
Did he have stage fright?

222
00:09:53,140 --> 00:09:54,280
Tell me in secret.

223
00:09:54,370 --> 00:09:56,040
During the transfer process,

224
00:09:56,130 --> 00:09:57,410
did he keep his eyes open

225
00:09:57,490 --> 00:09:58,990
or closed the whole time?

226
00:10:00,090 --> 00:10:01,060
Hello, Fali?

227
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:04,230
Don't do that.

228
00:10:04,530 --> 00:10:05,900
I've been trying
to figure something out for you.

229
00:10:05,990 --> 00:10:06,870
My brain is processing it.

230
00:10:06,950 --> 00:10:08,270
I may be spewing nonsense this whole time,

231
00:10:08,400 --> 00:10:09,550
but my brain has been working it out.

232
00:10:11,310 --> 00:10:14,390
Could it be quantum mechanics?

233
00:10:15,140 --> 00:10:16,900
In 1927,

234
00:10:16,980 --> 00:10:19,050
Heisenberg used his matrix mechanics

235
00:10:19,180 --> 00:10:20,720
and some theoretical experiments

236
00:10:20,810 --> 00:10:22,750
to come to an important conclusion

237
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:24,990
about matter and energy
on a microscopic level.

238
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:26,140
He found

239
00:10:26,220 --> 00:10:28,950
that in measuring
the particle momentum and its position,

240
00:10:29,040 --> 00:10:32,120
it would result
in the uncertainty principle.

241
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:35,860
It's fine if you're both not interested.

242
00:10:37,310 --> 00:10:38,370
To summarize,

243
00:10:39,030 --> 00:10:41,270
if kissing doesn't work,

244
00:10:41,620 --> 00:10:43,560
have you considered

245
00:10:43,650 --> 00:10:47,480
a more direct and deeper
physical interaction

246
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:50,160
than a kiss?

247
00:10:50,690 --> 00:10:51,520
Let's go.

248
00:10:52,050 --> 00:10:54,650
I'm kidding!

249
00:10:55,130 --> 00:10:55,790
Now,

250
00:10:56,360 --> 00:10:58,170
keep telling yourself

251
00:10:58,920 --> 00:11:01,290
that you want to go somewhere right now

252
00:11:01,690 --> 00:11:03,670
or you wish to see a certain person.

253
00:11:04,190 --> 00:11:05,070
Do you have the image?

254
00:11:05,470 --> 00:11:07,050
Yes, Lord Immortal.

255
00:11:07,540 --> 00:11:09,080
"Lord Immortal"?

256
00:11:09,170 --> 00:11:11,230
Why are you calling him that?

257
00:11:11,850 --> 00:11:15,280
Well, he's teaching me
the powers of an immortal.

258
00:11:15,630 --> 00:11:17,530
Shouldn't I show him some respect?

259
00:11:19,730 --> 00:11:20,740
Little girl, you're crushing it.

260
00:11:20,830 --> 00:11:21,840
Just ignore him and let's continue.

261
00:11:22,630 --> 00:11:24,920
The feeling of wanting to see that person,

262
00:11:25,050 --> 00:11:27,600
enlarge it and expand it.

263
00:11:28,350 --> 00:11:29,190
Believe in it.

264
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:32,130
Believe that when you open your eyes,

265
00:11:32,930 --> 00:11:34,600
you'll be there.

266
00:11:34,690 --> 00:11:36,800
You'll meet the person you want to see.

267
00:11:38,250 --> 00:11:40,410
I think I'm ready, Lord Immortal.

268
00:11:40,540 --> 00:11:41,290
Okay.

269
00:11:42,030 --> 00:11:44,370
Imagine the place you want to go to

270
00:11:44,540 --> 00:11:45,910
and the person you want to see.

271
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:47,970
How is it? Do you feel warm?

272
00:11:48,110 --> 00:11:49,120
Do you feel anything?

273
00:11:49,210 --> 00:11:50,310
You can say it.

274
00:11:51,010 --> 00:11:51,850
Do you?

275
00:11:52,370 --> 00:11:54,840
I don't feel warm.

276
00:11:55,060 --> 00:11:56,820
It's okay. Let's push harder.

277
00:11:56,910 --> 00:11:58,050
Imagine it with all your strength.

278
00:11:58,230 --> 00:11:59,980
"I want to go there."

279
00:12:00,070 --> 00:12:00,910
"I want to see him."

280
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:02,400
Enlarge it and expand it.

281
00:12:02,490 --> 00:12:04,300
In the end,
you want to see them so much that...

282
00:12:04,380 --> 00:12:06,540
Forget it. Let's go home and rest.

283
00:12:07,070 --> 00:12:10,240
'Orad! We haven't even started yet.

284
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:11,910
Why are you already giving up?

285
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:14,810
It's okay. I think I can keep going.

286
00:12:15,560 --> 00:12:16,570
See? Did you see that?

287
00:12:16,700 --> 00:12:18,160
Let's try again, Lord Immortal.

288
00:12:19,520 --> 00:12:22,420
Little girl, I think you've changed.

289
00:12:22,510 --> 00:12:24,360
You've become more positive.

290
00:12:26,520 --> 00:12:28,670
It's because if I can't return the powers

291
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:30,960
back to 'Orad,

292
00:12:31,050 --> 00:12:31,800
I might be able

293
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:33,380
to help Chen Ai-ting

294
00:12:34,480 --> 00:12:36,990
if I learn how to use them.

295
00:12:37,120 --> 00:12:38,310
I want to help her see again.

296
00:12:39,630 --> 00:12:40,510
Chen Ai-ting.

297
00:12:42,270 --> 00:12:45,570
Chen Ai-ting.

298
00:12:45,920 --> 00:12:47,550
Chen Ai-ting probably

299
00:12:47,640 --> 00:12:49,220
doesn't need it anymore.

300
00:12:50,320 --> 00:12:51,550
What do you mean?

301
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:52,520
Well...

302
00:12:53,750 --> 00:12:56,390
Didn't you ask me to visit them before?

303
00:12:56,830 --> 00:12:59,430
In the brief moment when I zoned out,
Fali made his move.

304
00:13:01,050 --> 00:13:02,550
So what happened to them?

305
00:13:03,780 --> 00:13:05,010
They...

306
00:13:05,100 --> 00:13:07,170
Fali had altered their memories.

307
00:13:07,260 --> 00:13:07,920
So now,

308
00:13:08,010 --> 00:13:09,990
they won't remember either of you.

309
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:12,540
But it's okay because the Department
of Social Welfare stepped in.

310
00:13:12,630 --> 00:13:14,210
They found them new families too.

311
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:15,310
So you don't need to worry.

312
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:17,290
The most important thing right now is you.

313
00:13:17,550 --> 00:13:18,870
I'm certain that Fali came back

314
00:13:18,960 --> 00:13:21,470
because of you two.

315
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:24,640
Okay, guys. It's okay.

316
00:13:24,770 --> 00:13:26,490
Let's continue, shall we?

317
00:13:32,780 --> 00:13:34,850
If I'm not mistaken,

318
00:13:35,950 --> 00:13:37,970
the Fali you talked about

319
00:13:38,060 --> 00:13:39,860
is the owner of New World Horizon,

320
00:13:39,950 --> 00:13:41,180
Sung Hsiao-feng.

321
00:13:42,150 --> 00:13:42,720
Am I right?

322
00:13:46,370 --> 00:13:48,660
Can you tell me about him now?

323
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:55,300
He is the head of
the Cause and Effect Correction Bureau.

324
00:13:57,240 --> 00:13:59,350
What exactly is
the Cause and Effect Correction Bureau?

325
00:14:00,450 --> 00:14:02,260
The Cause and Effect Correction Bureau

326
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:05,250
exists to correct

327
00:14:05,340 --> 00:14:08,020
anything that goes against
the will of Kakarayan.

328
00:14:11,230 --> 00:14:13,390
And by "correct,"

329
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:14,880
does it include altering memories too?

330
00:14:21,090 --> 00:14:23,950
After I told you that I liked you
five years ago,

331
00:14:25,090 --> 00:14:26,760
he was the one who appeared

332
00:14:26,900 --> 00:14:28,740
and erased my memory of you

333
00:14:29,670 --> 00:14:32,350
and your existence.

334
00:14:33,140 --> 00:14:33,850
Am I right?

335
00:14:38,640 --> 00:14:39,740
I thought

336
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:41,770
you were the one who erased my memory.

337
00:14:42,520 --> 00:14:43,750
But seeing Sung Hsiao-feng that day

338
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:46,560
at the office brought it all back.

339
00:14:46,650 --> 00:14:48,890
It wasn't you. It was him.

340
00:14:49,690 --> 00:14:50,790
I don't know who he is,

341
00:14:50,870 --> 00:14:52,850
why he did that,

342
00:14:52,990 --> 00:14:55,630
or why he erased my memories of us.

343
00:14:56,590 --> 00:14:58,090
That's why in the last two days,

344
00:14:58,180 --> 00:15:00,510
I kept thinking

345
00:15:01,350 --> 00:15:03,330
about what we've been through.

346
00:15:05,390 --> 00:15:07,020
[I remembered a lot of episodes]

347
00:15:09,130 --> 00:15:11,860
[that we shared a long time ago.]

348
00:15:12,790 --> 00:15:15,470
[After replaying those images
in my mind again and again,]

349
00:15:17,800 --> 00:15:19,340
I finally understood

350
00:15:23,790 --> 00:15:25,940
why I spoke to you

351
00:15:27,350 --> 00:15:29,110
the way I did back then

352
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,590
and why I looked at you that way.

353
00:15:36,280 --> 00:15:37,250
So Fali removed

354
00:15:37,340 --> 00:15:39,630
the memories of you and me

355
00:15:40,770 --> 00:15:42,700
because I can't like you?

356
00:15:53,350 --> 00:15:54,360
Hinapeloh.

357
00:15:55,380 --> 00:15:56,610
Do you know

358
00:15:56,700 --> 00:15:59,690
why I left Pinokayan and came back here?

359
00:15:59,780 --> 00:16:01,050
I know.

360
00:16:01,180 --> 00:16:02,370
You were going to take
the rest of the Kawas

361
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:03,960
back to Pinokayan.

362
00:16:04,090 --> 00:16:05,580
If you knew that,

363
00:16:05,720 --> 00:16:07,650
why did you still appear before me?

364
00:16:07,740 --> 00:16:09,680
There was a reason
why I had to come to you.

365
00:16:10,470 --> 00:16:13,460
I saw a Papa' orip
that brought death to mankind.

366
00:16:17,510 --> 00:16:19,970
That Papa' orip was different
from the other Kariah.

367
00:16:20,100 --> 00:16:22,520
He didn't have the red eyes of a Kariah.

368
00:16:22,610 --> 00:16:24,500
So he didn't know the amount of damage

369
00:16:24,640 --> 00:16:27,410
his actions would cause to humankind.

370
00:16:27,500 --> 00:16:29,920
I appeared before you

371
00:16:30,710 --> 00:16:33,390
because I want to meet with Kakarayan.

372
00:16:35,410 --> 00:16:40,470
I want to ask Kakarayan
to stop that Papa' orip.

373
00:16:40,610 --> 00:16:42,760
Kakarayan is no longer here.

374
00:16:44,650 --> 00:16:45,530
You won't be able to find Him

375
00:16:45,670 --> 00:16:46,940
in this world.

376
00:16:47,030 --> 00:16:47,870
I know Kakarayan took back

377
00:16:47,950 --> 00:16:49,930
all the blessings He once gave
to the human world.

378
00:16:50,070 --> 00:16:51,740
All the Kawas had also returned.

379
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,280
So Fali,

380
00:16:54,470 --> 00:16:55,830
do what you're supposed to do.

381
00:16:56,310 --> 00:16:57,990
Take me back to Pinokayan.

382
00:16:58,340 --> 00:17:00,270
Let me plead with Kakarayan myself.

383
00:17:00,360 --> 00:17:01,240
Can I?

384
00:17:04,940 --> 00:17:05,510
Okay.

385
00:17:06,650 --> 00:17:07,670
I'll do that.

386
00:17:08,589 --> 00:17:10,569
I'll send you back to Pinokayan.

387
00:17:21,220 --> 00:17:23,680
Once you walk through this door,

388
00:17:24,250 --> 00:17:27,329
you'll be able to meet Kakarayan

389
00:17:28,390 --> 00:17:32,480
and talk to Him yourself.

390
00:18:13,220 --> 00:18:16,570
Using the company's computer
to browse job sites.

391
00:18:16,660 --> 00:18:17,670
If my mom finds out,

392
00:18:17,760 --> 00:18:18,460
you'll be dead meat.

393
00:18:18,550 --> 00:18:19,560
Don't talk nonsense.

394
00:18:19,650 --> 00:18:21,360
I was watching the news.

395
00:18:21,500 --> 00:18:22,600
[Recently, news of multiple infections
of unknown origin]

396
00:18:22,730 --> 00:18:24,710
[have popped up around Taipei.]

397
00:18:23,300 --> 00:18:26,910
[Seven people have died so far
from the unknown disease]

398
00:18:24,800 --> 00:18:26,860
[So far, it has been reported
that 36 patients]

399
00:18:26,990 --> 00:18:29,060
[have been taken to the hospital
after they suddenly fainted.]

400
00:18:29,150 --> 00:18:30,070
[Upon arrival at the hospital,]

401
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:31,790
[the patients were found
in a state of unconsciousness,]

402
00:18:31,880 --> 00:18:32,800
[low blood pressure,]

403
00:18:32,890 --> 00:18:34,780
[and even signs of organ failure.]

404
00:18:34,870 --> 00:18:36,850
Mom, come and look at this.

405
00:18:36,940 --> 00:18:38,350
-What is it?
[-The source of infection is unknown.]

406
00:18:38,480 --> 00:18:40,410
[The Centers for Disease Control
and Prevention announced]

407
00:18:40,550 --> 00:18:42,880
[that they will take
relevant countermeasures promptly.]

408
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:42,530
[Seven people have died so far
from the unknown disease]

409
00:18:43,010 --> 00:18:45,780
It looks like this epidemic
is getting worse.

410
00:18:46,310 --> 00:18:49,040
Did we get any cancelation today?

411
00:18:49,130 --> 00:18:50,180
No.

412
00:18:51,810 --> 00:18:53,130
What's wrong with this world?

413
00:18:53,220 --> 00:18:55,550
First the weather, then the food crisis.

414
00:18:55,640 --> 00:18:57,180
And now, this weird disease.

415
00:18:59,690 --> 00:19:00,610
[So Fali removed]

416
00:19:00,700 --> 00:19:02,500
[the memories of you and me]

417
00:19:02,630 --> 00:19:05,190
because I can't like you?

418
00:19:17,420 --> 00:19:19,310
I can't protect you right now.

419
00:19:20,410 --> 00:19:21,950
So don't ask anymore

420
00:19:22,520 --> 00:19:23,970
and stop thinking about it.

421
00:19:26,390 --> 00:19:27,540
It's all in the past.

422
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:38,360
Mr. Sung, what brings you here so early?

423
00:19:38,840 --> 00:19:41,310
It has been a while. How have you been?

424
00:19:41,440 --> 00:19:44,040
Hsiao-feng, why didn't you call first?

425
00:19:44,170 --> 00:19:44,780
Pu.

426
00:19:44,870 --> 00:19:45,750
Prepare the triple-A grade coffee.

427
00:19:45,840 --> 00:19:47,070
It's okay.

428
00:19:47,200 --> 00:19:48,570
I'm here to tell you

429
00:19:48,660 --> 00:19:50,150
that I won't be the one

430
00:19:50,280 --> 00:19:51,120
you'll be presenting the itinerary to.

431
00:19:59,830 --> 00:20:01,720
The girl you're meeting later

432
00:20:01,860 --> 00:20:03,700
is the one I mentioned before.

433
00:20:03,790 --> 00:20:05,240
She has undergone five major surgeries

434
00:20:05,330 --> 00:20:07,000
because of her heart condition.

435
00:20:07,090 --> 00:20:09,340
She spent most of her childhood
in the hospital.

436
00:20:09,470 --> 00:20:10,700
Forget about traveling,

437
00:20:10,790 --> 00:20:12,200
even going to school like a normal student

438
00:20:12,280 --> 00:20:13,820
is a luxury.

439
00:20:14,790 --> 00:20:16,110
How cool.

440
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:18,220
She has gotten better lately.

441
00:20:18,310 --> 00:20:20,470
So the foundation, her doctor,

442
00:20:20,550 --> 00:20:21,870
and her parents decided

443
00:20:22,010 --> 00:20:24,820
to give her a special trip.

444
00:20:38,020 --> 00:20:40,090
Sung-en, Mrs. Lu.

445
00:20:40,180 --> 00:20:40,620
Hello.

446
00:20:40,710 --> 00:20:41,810
Hello.

447
00:20:41,940 --> 00:20:43,430
Let me introduce you.

448
00:20:43,960 --> 00:20:45,810
This is Lu Sung-en.

449
00:20:45,900 --> 00:20:47,790
This is Sung-en's mom.

450
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:49,640
Hello, Sung-en and Mrs. Lu.

451
00:20:49,770 --> 00:20:51,660
The weather is nice, it looks hot.

452
00:20:51,750 --> 00:20:53,380
Yes, it was so hot that day.

453
00:20:53,470 --> 00:20:55,090
She was sweating so much.

454
00:20:55,180 --> 00:20:57,690
I told her to tie her hair up,
but she refused.

455
00:20:57,780 --> 00:20:59,320
Can I ask you something, miss?

456
00:20:59,410 --> 00:21:01,210
How long have you been
growing your hair out?

457
00:21:01,300 --> 00:21:02,000
Hsieh Tien-ti.

458
00:21:02,350 --> 00:21:03,230
Hsieh Tien-ti.

459
00:21:03,320 --> 00:21:04,510
I'm Hsieh Tien-ti.

460
00:21:05,570 --> 00:21:07,770
Sung-en, how are you feeling today?

461
00:21:08,210 --> 00:21:09,170
What do you think?

462
00:21:09,530 --> 00:21:10,580
I think

463
00:21:11,110 --> 00:21:13,040
you look great.

464
00:21:13,130 --> 00:21:14,140
If you weren't in the hospital,

465
00:21:14,230 --> 00:21:15,860
I wouldn't have guessed you were sick.

466
00:21:15,990 --> 00:21:16,960
Right?

467
00:21:17,050 --> 00:21:19,200
You should say that to my doctor.

468
00:21:19,290 --> 00:21:21,140
I've always thought that I'm fine.

469
00:21:21,270 --> 00:21:23,080
If this trip goes well,

470
00:21:23,160 --> 00:21:25,010
I think I can go back to school.

471
00:21:25,140 --> 00:21:25,940
Actually, Sung-en

472
00:21:26,020 --> 00:21:27,780
fainted once two months ago.

473
00:21:27,870 --> 00:21:30,120
That's why I'm counting on you

474
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:31,700
to keep an eye on her during the trip.

475
00:21:31,790 --> 00:21:33,020
Don't worry, Mrs. Lu.

476
00:21:33,110 --> 00:21:34,780
When we were planning the trip,

477
00:21:34,870 --> 00:21:37,420
we took Sung-en's condition
into consideration.

478
00:21:38,170 --> 00:21:40,060
Would you like
to go through the itinerary?

479
00:21:40,190 --> 00:21:41,600
If you have any concerns

480
00:21:41,690 --> 00:21:42,920
or if Sung-en has any thoughts,

481
00:21:43,010 --> 00:21:44,020
you can tell me.

482
00:21:44,110 --> 00:21:44,770
Of course

483
00:21:44,860 --> 00:21:46,970
if Mr. Sung has something to tell me,

484
00:21:47,100 --> 00:21:48,070
it's okay too.

485
00:21:48,200 --> 00:21:50,270
I'm sorry, but I have a meeting.

486
00:21:50,360 --> 00:21:53,170
Just brief Sung-en about it.

487
00:21:53,880 --> 00:21:54,800
You're leaving?

488
00:21:54,930 --> 00:21:55,770
I told you.

489
00:21:55,900 --> 00:21:57,530
I'm not the target of today's briefing.

490
00:21:57,970 --> 00:22:00,340
Sung-en, I'll leave the rest

491
00:22:00,480 --> 00:22:01,880
to you.

492
00:22:02,020 --> 00:22:02,850
Is that okay?

493
00:22:02,980 --> 00:22:04,390
Sure.

494
00:22:04,960 --> 00:22:05,580
I'll be off then.

495
00:22:05,710 --> 00:22:06,420
Thank you.

496
00:22:17,410 --> 00:22:19,130
Wu Yi-han, explain to them first.

497
00:22:19,260 --> 00:22:20,490
I'll be right back.

498
00:22:24,720 --> 00:22:26,870
Where is she going?

499
00:22:29,600 --> 00:22:32,460
You see, they have something urgent to do.

500
00:22:32,550 --> 00:22:34,750
Let me go through

501
00:22:34,880 --> 00:22:36,690
the itinerary with you.

502
00:22:36,820 --> 00:22:39,280
Okay, thank you.

503
00:22:39,370 --> 00:22:41,390
It looks good.

504
00:22:42,800 --> 00:22:44,690
Wait, Mr. Sung.

505
00:22:50,190 --> 00:22:53,190
Did you arrange this trip because of me?

506
00:22:54,290 --> 00:22:57,060
I know you're a Kawas just like 'Orad.

507
00:22:57,630 --> 00:23:00,530
You're in charge of correcting
the cause and effect.

508
00:23:01,980 --> 00:23:03,260
I think you're mistaken.

509
00:23:03,350 --> 00:23:06,340
I'm not doing this just because of you.

510
00:23:06,470 --> 00:23:07,570
It's about making sure

511
00:23:07,660 --> 00:23:10,480
the cause and effect proceeds
according to Kakarayan's plan.

512
00:23:10,560 --> 00:23:12,980
I'm sorry to say this.

513
00:23:13,070 --> 00:23:14,700
Lu Sung-en, whom you've just met,

514
00:23:14,790 --> 00:23:16,060
will die of a heart attack

515
00:23:16,150 --> 00:23:18,840
in the near future.

516
00:23:20,330 --> 00:23:22,360
[Make way!]

517
00:23:23,680 --> 00:23:25,570
Has the family been notified?

518
00:23:25,660 --> 00:23:26,710
Yes, we've notified them.

519
00:23:27,420 --> 00:23:28,690
[The original order of cause and effect]

520
00:23:28,780 --> 00:23:30,630
[wasn't supposed to be like this.]

521
00:23:30,720 --> 00:23:31,860
Because...

522
00:23:31,990 --> 00:23:34,810
in the original plan of Kakarayan,

523
00:23:34,900 --> 00:23:36,740
she gets a heart transplant surgery

524
00:23:36,880 --> 00:23:38,370
and becomes healthy again.

525
00:23:38,460 --> 00:23:40,530
She gets to live out her life.

526
00:23:42,110 --> 00:23:44,400
But it all changed

527
00:23:44,490 --> 00:23:46,070
because of one person.

528
00:23:49,900 --> 00:23:52,100
[That accident won't take your life.]

529
00:23:53,420 --> 00:23:54,560
It will only make you

530
00:23:55,310 --> 00:23:56,900
unable to wake up again.

531
00:23:59,310 --> 00:24:01,290
Two hours after the accident,

532
00:24:01,870 --> 00:24:04,200
you will undergo
a heart transplant operation.

533
00:24:06,090 --> 00:24:07,980
A heart transplant?

534
00:24:09,830 --> 00:24:10,840
Due to brain death,

535
00:24:10,970 --> 00:24:13,880
you'll donate your heart
to another sick person.

536
00:24:17,180 --> 00:24:18,980
After the surgery,

537
00:24:19,690 --> 00:24:21,490
you are then officially pronounced dead.

538
00:24:22,850 --> 00:24:25,450
But thanks to you,
another life will be saved.

539
00:24:27,910 --> 00:24:31,700
So if I don't die,

540
00:24:32,490 --> 00:24:34,910
what will happen to that person?

541
00:24:39,270 --> 00:24:41,420
You don't have
to look at me like that, 'Orad.

542
00:24:41,510 --> 00:24:43,180
As the messenger of Kakarayan,

543
00:24:43,270 --> 00:24:44,900
I'm sure you already know

544
00:24:45,030 --> 00:24:46,610
that Lu Sung-en is the one

545
00:24:46,700 --> 00:24:48,200
who gets to live

546
00:24:48,330 --> 00:24:50,130
after receiving Hsieh Tien-ti's heart.

547
00:24:55,190 --> 00:24:56,380
Hsieh Tien-ti.

548
00:24:57,740 --> 00:24:59,280
Do you see

549
00:24:59,370 --> 00:25:01,000
why I have to correct
the changes you made?

550
00:25:03,680 --> 00:25:04,830
In my opinion,

551
00:25:04,920 --> 00:25:07,160
it's not that you want
to change your fate.

552
00:25:07,250 --> 00:25:08,610
In fact,

553
00:25:09,930 --> 00:25:12,530
you just want to live

554
00:25:14,200 --> 00:25:16,750
at the expense of someone else's future.

555
00:25:37,430 --> 00:25:38,620
[Do you know why]

556
00:25:38,270 --> 00:26:08,230
[Next episode]

557
00:25:38,710 --> 00:25:40,030
[there is no "sorry"]

558
00:25:40,120 --> 00:25:41,440
[in the language of the Kawas?]

559
00:25:42,050 --> 00:25:43,060
[I'm a human.]

560
00:25:43,200 --> 00:25:44,780
[I'm not a Kawas.]

561
00:25:44,870 --> 00:25:46,100
You will never know

562
00:25:46,230 --> 00:25:47,640
how painful it is for us

563
00:25:47,770 --> 00:25:49,400
who are living through it.

564
00:25:49,620 --> 00:25:52,040
[The one who ruined this world]

565
00:25:52,170 --> 00:25:53,310
is not the humans.

566
00:25:53,450 --> 00:25:54,550
It's God.

567
00:25:54,630 --> 00:25:56,310
[I really can't let you
go see her right now.]

568
00:25:56,480 --> 00:25:57,270
Move aside.

569
00:26:01,590 --> 00:26:03,830
[You mean that if I die,]

570
00:26:05,280 --> 00:26:07,260
[the girl can live?]

571
00:26:08,490 --> 00:26:11,220
[Wu Yi-han, Mountain Travel, May 2016
2016, There is someone I like]

572
00:26:11,350 --> 00:26:12,890
[Wang Ting-yi, Mountain Travel, May 2016]

573
00:26:18,660 --> 00:26:19,890
I'll go home now.

574
00:26:20,330 --> 00:26:21,210
Bye.

575
00:26:23,370 --> 00:26:24,380
Ssu-chieh.

576
00:26:24,510 --> 00:26:26,010
Hi, are you leaving?

577
00:26:26,090 --> 00:26:27,330
Do you want to eat something?

578
00:26:28,290 --> 00:26:30,140
No, you guys go ahead.

579
00:26:30,270 --> 00:26:31,730
Go in then.

580
00:26:32,390 --> 00:26:34,890
Bye, Tien-ti. I'm off.

581
00:26:34,980 --> 00:26:36,430
You guys chat slowly.

582
00:26:36,520 --> 00:26:38,020
Bye.

583
00:26:41,050 --> 00:26:42,020
What brings you here?

584
00:26:42,150 --> 00:26:43,030
I passed by your office

585
00:26:43,120 --> 00:26:44,920
and brought some food.

586
00:26:45,540 --> 00:26:46,730
Thank you.

587
00:26:46,860 --> 00:26:47,960
Is no one else here?

588
00:26:48,090 --> 00:26:49,280
Yes.

589
00:26:49,370 --> 00:26:50,820
Where is Ms. Chang-fen?

590
00:26:51,260 --> 00:26:53,900
She's on a business trip,
so she didn't come in today.

591
00:26:57,070 --> 00:26:58,170
How have you been?

592
00:26:58,870 --> 00:27:00,540
Same old, same old.

593
00:27:01,690 --> 00:27:04,550
But there's one thing

594
00:27:05,250 --> 00:27:07,360
that has been stuck in my heart.

595
00:27:08,200 --> 00:27:09,740
It's about

596
00:27:09,830 --> 00:27:11,590
what I asked you last time.

597
00:27:12,120 --> 00:27:13,390
Have you thought about it?

598
00:27:17,620 --> 00:27:19,330
I've thought about it.

599
00:27:21,180 --> 00:27:22,410
Then...

600
00:27:23,600 --> 00:27:24,390
I'm sorry.

601
00:27:29,450 --> 00:27:31,560
I think

602
00:27:33,630 --> 00:27:35,040
I'm not ready.

603
00:27:36,270 --> 00:27:37,330
It's okay.

604
00:27:37,810 --> 00:27:41,020
You can't force love.

605
00:27:42,080 --> 00:27:43,000
I get it.

606
00:27:45,910 --> 00:27:46,790
I'm sorry.

607
00:27:47,970 --> 00:27:49,250
Stop apologizing to me.

608
00:27:49,340 --> 00:27:51,190
You didn't do anything wrong.

609
00:27:51,270 --> 00:27:53,690
But what I want to know is,

610
00:27:53,830 --> 00:27:56,070
did you turn me down

611
00:27:56,200 --> 00:27:58,140
because you don't like me?

612
00:27:58,800 --> 00:28:00,910
Or do you already have someone you like?

613
00:28:02,540 --> 00:28:03,900
Someone I like?

614
00:28:06,370 --> 00:28:07,600
There's none.

615
00:28:07,470 --> 00:28:15,250
[Mountain Travel]

616
00:28:08,430 --> 00:28:09,620
There's no one.

617
00:28:20,710 --> 00:28:22,470
Are you okay?

618
00:28:41,740 --> 00:28:43,320
Excuse me.

619
00:28:45,790 --> 00:28:48,690
I don't know why I'm like this.

620
00:28:51,290 --> 00:28:53,530
From now on,

621
00:28:53,620 --> 00:28:55,560
you'll forget

622
00:28:56,440 --> 00:28:58,330
everything about that person.
